adjudication.rationale:
In `EventManager.createAllCalendarEvents`, the new loop iterates over every `destination` in `event.destinationCalendar`. For destinations without `credentialId`, it executes:

```ts
const destinationCalendarCredentials = this.calendarCredentials.filter(
  (c) => c.type === destination.integration
);
createdEvents = createdEvents.concat(
  await Promise.all(destinationCalendarCredentials.map(async (c) => await createEvent(c, event)))
);
```

This means each such destination triggers `createEvent` for *every* matching credential. If there are multiple legacy destination entries of the same `integration` without `credentialId`, this code repeats the same per-credential fan-out for each entry, multiplying external API calls and likely creating duplicate events (notably, it also doesn’t pass `destination.externalId` into `createEvent` in this branch, so calendar selection can’t be scoped to a specific destination).
